1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,850
Welcome to the PEN-Plus
NCD Monitoring App.

2
00:00:06,380 --> 00:00:13,040
Mentors use this app to observe
and assess their mentees.

3
00:00:15,379 --> 00:00:22,500
This is the home screen, the first
thing you see after opening the app.

4
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:32,500
The app is designed for tablets, but it works
on any device: a computer, laptop or phone.

5
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:38,700
It also works offline, without
an internet connection.

6
00:00:39,760 --> 00:00:51,640
Once you're connected, it syncs
automatically, or you can sync manually.

7
00:00:51,640 --> 00:01:00,340
At the top are the two main buttons.

8
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:06,740
This one starts a new session.

9
00:01:09,520 --> 00:01:18,500
This outlined one shows all
the mentees available to you.

10
00:01:22,620 --> 00:01:30,940
Below them, "Continue where you left
off" lists your journeys in progress,

11
00:01:33,520 --> 00:01:39,680
so you can quickly start another
session or round with a mentee.

12
00:01:40,780 --> 00:01:49,720
Next are the open gaps that
need to be followed up.

13
00:01:50,820 --> 00:01:54,400
Then come your most recent sessions.

14
00:01:56,260 --> 00:02:05,140
A good place to start is My
Mentees, the button on the right.

15
00:02:05,780 --> 00:02:11,320
This is the list of all the
mentees available to you.

16
00:02:12,680 --> 00:02:29,200
Each card shows the mentee's
name, profession and district,

17
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:32,100
their facility, and
the number of sessions.

18
00:02:32,120 --> 00:02:43,740
Tapping a mentee opens their profile.

19
00:02:47,440 --> 00:02:51,960
It lists the mentee's evaluation journeys.

20
00:02:52,480 --> 00:03:05,560
A journey is one mentee's progress
on one clinical tool over time,

21
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:08,320
and each mentorship visit
is recorded as a session.

22
00:03:09,440 --> 00:03:16,380
Demo Mentee 002 has four journeys so far,

23
00:03:16,380 --> 00:03:21,900
meaning they've been evaluated
on four different tools.

24
00:03:22,760 --> 00:03:30,600
This Epilepsy journey has six
sessions, and this one has four.

25
00:03:36,680 --> 00:03:44,740
A journey is the path to
basic competency on a tool.

26
00:03:45,840 --> 00:03:48,540
That's why we call it a journey.

27
00:03:49,900 --> 00:04:01,860
In Respiratory Diseases, this mentee is now
fully competent: they've reached the destination.

28
00:04:02,060 --> 00:04:14,340
Every competency item in that
journey now scores 4 or 5.

29
00:04:16,140 --> 00:04:20,600
To go back, use the Back
button in the header.

30
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:35,820
Now let's run a session with a
mentee who hasn't had one yet.

31
00:04:36,220 --> 00:04:40,260
I've created Demo Mentee XYZ,
so I'll search for them here.

32
00:04:40,860 --> 00:04:47,880
Demo Mentee XYZ has no sessions
yet, so let's assess them.

33
00:04:49,220 --> 00:04:56,140
Their profile opens, with the
green Start New Session button.

34
00:04:57,200 --> 00:05:00,100
Let's tap it.

35
00:05:02,940 --> 00:05:11,660
Here we choose the clinical
tool for the evaluation.

36
00:05:12,880 --> 00:05:19,800
Let's go with Diabetes Mellitus.

37
00:05:20,820 --> 00:05:24,720
Selecting it takes us
to the planning step,

38
00:05:24,780 --> 00:05:27,340
where we plan today's mentoring.

39
00:05:28,040 --> 00:05:34,860
The app shows we're in step one: planning.

40
00:05:35,160 --> 00:05:40,140
Here we choose the items
we want to observe today.

41
00:05:41,240 --> 00:05:46,840
The mentee's name and the
tool are shown at the top.

42
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:53,200
This is the date. It defaults to today,

43
00:05:54,080 --> 00:06:05,060
but you can choose any date, for example when entering
a session after it took place rather than live.

44
00:06:06,620 --> 00:06:09,360
The app supports both.

45
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:15,460
We'll keep today's date, then
choose the mentorship phase.

46
00:06:18,100 --> 00:06:21,760
As this is the first session,
we'll choose Initial Intensive.

47
00:06:23,040 --> 00:06:34,000
These are all the competency
items for Diabetes Mellitus.

48
00:06:34,720 --> 00:06:43,680
They're grouped into the same
sections as the paper tool.

49
00:06:44,620 --> 00:06:49,760
Patient Assessment and Classification,
for example, has three items,

50
00:06:50,160 --> 00:06:59,740
and Treatment Adjustment and
Individualization for Type 1 DM has eight.

51
00:07:01,680 --> 00:07:14,600
When planning, Select all picks
every item in a section in one tap.

52
00:07:17,120 --> 00:07:22,540
But you don't need to observe
everything in one day.

53
00:07:24,640 --> 00:07:30,300
So you can clear a section and
select only the items you need.

54
00:07:30,860 --> 00:07:39,600
Let's choose one item here, two
here, and skip the other sections.

55
00:07:39,740 --> 00:07:43,100
In Patient Education,
we'll choose a couple.

56
00:07:44,900 --> 00:07:48,920
Next are the general
counselling competencies.

57
00:07:49,600 --> 00:07:59,780
They appear on every tool, not just
Diabetes, whichever tool you choose.

58
00:07:59,880 --> 00:08:05,040
If you don't want to assess
them, just clear them.

59
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:15,060
You can select all of them, or only
some. Here, we'll assess three.

60
00:08:16,800 --> 00:08:20,440
We've now selected eight
Diabetes Mellitus items.

61
00:08:22,040 --> 00:08:29,540
If we're happy with today's
plan, we tap Confirm plan.

62
00:08:30,280 --> 00:08:35,220
This takes us to step two: observation.

63
00:08:36,500 --> 00:08:43,980
The items we selected in the
plan are now ready to be scored.

64
00:08:46,960 --> 00:08:54,400
The date and the Initial Intensive
phase are set, and here are the rounds.

65
00:08:56,780 --> 00:09:00,780
A session can include as many
observation rounds as needed.

66
00:09:01,320 --> 00:09:08,180
For example, you might observe the
mentee in a round in the morning,

67
00:09:09,080 --> 00:09:13,760
then do one or two more
rounds in the afternoon,

68
00:09:13,820 --> 00:09:17,640
and another in the evening
when a new patient arrives.

69
00:09:18,840 --> 00:09:23,880
For the first round, the app
selects Round 1 automatically.

70
00:09:26,640 --> 00:09:31,660
The score legend guides the scoring.

71
00:09:32,460 --> 00:09:38,720
1 is red, 2 is orange,
3 is yellow, and so on,

72
00:09:38,880 --> 00:09:42,840
and the legend explains
what each score means.

73
00:09:45,580 --> 00:09:47,520
Now let's score.

74
00:09:48,880 --> 00:09:51,100
This item gets a 3.

75
00:09:51,780 --> 00:10:01,960
When you tap a score, the app shows
the score given and what it means.

76
00:10:02,780 --> 00:10:13,060
A 4, for example, means the mentee
demonstrates advanced competency.

77
00:10:15,560 --> 00:10:18,780
Next: "Safely titrates
insulin for Ramadan".

78
00:10:21,240 --> 00:10:23,300
We'll give a 1. They didn't do well.

79
00:10:23,860 --> 00:10:25,640
You can also add a note to any item.

80
00:10:36,800 --> 00:10:42,560
The items are still grouped
by section, as in the plan.

81
00:10:43,900 --> 00:10:51,420
To save time, let's give the general
counselling items quick scores.

82
00:10:52,340 --> 00:10:54,060
This one gets a 2.

83
00:10:54,420 --> 00:10:56,440
If you choose N/A, meaning not applicable,

84
00:10:59,980 --> 00:11:03,360
add a note explaining why
it couldn't be evaluated.

85
00:11:03,940 --> 00:11:11,420
For example: "The facility doesn't
have the required equipment."

86
00:11:14,500 --> 00:11:24,310
When you've finished scoring, you can
add overall notes for the whole session.

87
00:11:26,140 --> 00:11:29,320
For example: "All went well."

88
00:11:30,740 --> 00:11:36,260
When you're done, tap Review session.

89
00:11:38,280 --> 00:11:45,960
At this point, the session
has not been saved yet.

90
00:11:47,440 --> 00:11:53,340
That gives you a chance to check
for mistakes and go back to edit.

91
00:11:55,060 --> 00:12:04,500
The review gives an overview
of the session and its rounds.

92
00:12:05,060 --> 00:12:14,340
Here, three required items need a
score of 4 or 5, but are below that.

93
00:12:14,660 --> 00:12:20,740
The review lists them,
with the scores given.

94
00:12:22,440 --> 00:12:32,620
It also shows how many items were scored,
how many were marked N/A, and the averages.

95
00:12:35,980 --> 00:12:40,400
Everything looks right.
These are the scores we gave.

96
00:12:43,620 --> 00:12:50,360
If you spot a wrong score,
say on D32, you can go back.

97
00:12:53,080 --> 00:13:01,640
Open D32 and change the score.
They did better, so we'll give a 5.

98
00:13:02,720 --> 00:13:05,100
Then return to Review session.

99
00:13:06,580 --> 00:13:13,040
D32 is no longer listed as
below 4, and now shows a 5.

100
00:13:14,900 --> 00:13:21,000
Everything is correct,
so we tap Save Session.

101
00:13:21,620 --> 00:13:24,740
The session is now saved.

102
00:13:26,340 --> 00:13:33,540
Once synced to the server, it can be analysed in
the reporting platform, which we'll cover later.

103
00:13:35,440 --> 00:13:42,420
This is the session we've just recorded,
now a journey for Demo Mentee XYZ.

104
00:13:42,560 --> 00:13:46,840
Earlier there were no
journeys. Now there is one.

105
00:13:48,720 --> 00:13:55,060
So that's how a session works:
plan first, then observe,

106
00:13:56,560 --> 00:14:03,440
then review, and if
everything is right, save.

107
00:14:05,840 --> 00:14:12,540
Coming back days or even months later,
you can check on Demo Mentee XYZ.

108
00:14:13,640 --> 00:14:20,660
Just tap the journey to see what happened.

109
00:14:20,900 --> 00:14:30,740
The summary shows one session, an average
score of 3.4, recorded on 17 October.

110
00:14:30,860 --> 00:14:42,140
To edit a session, open it and tap Edit.

111
00:14:46,040 --> 00:14:49,300
Let's change this score to a 2.

112
00:14:50,340 --> 00:14:52,040
Review the session again,

113
00:14:54,840 --> 00:14:59,020
check the 2 we just gave,
and tap Save Session.

114
00:15:02,960 --> 00:15:08,260
Now let's log a gap: an area
the mentee needs to work on.

115
00:15:09,140 --> 00:15:16,240
Open the journey and tap Log
Gap, and this form appears.

116
00:15:17,500 --> 00:15:19,180
Here's how to log a gap.

117
00:15:20,240 --> 00:15:28,880
Description: "Did not
perform titration well."

118
00:15:30,360 --> 00:15:32,780
Domain: clinical skills.

119
00:15:34,620 --> 00:15:39,120
Was it addressed in this session?
No, it will be covered later.

120
00:15:39,120 --> 00:15:57,900
Target timeline: the next
session, on 24 October 2026.

121
00:16:06,220 --> 00:16:08,200
Then tap Log Gap.

122
00:16:09,340 --> 00:16:15,040
That completes the session.

123
00:16:19,420 --> 00:16:24,700
Tap here to return to the home screen.

124
00:16:27,580 --> 00:16:36,940
The journey now appears here,
along with the gap we just logged.

125
00:16:37,120 --> 00:16:44,580
Next, another tool that's worth showing.

126
00:16:44,580 --> 00:16:57,320
From My Mentees, let's choose
a mentee for Echocardiogram.

127
00:16:58,060 --> 00:17:04,240
This mentee already has two
Echocardiogram sessions.

128
00:17:04,339 --> 00:17:08,760
We start a new session
and choose Echocardiogram.

129
00:17:10,980 --> 00:17:13,220
You can see the two previous sessions.

130
00:17:14,319 --> 00:17:16,020
Again, we begin with planning.

131
00:17:16,720 --> 00:17:27,660
We'll choose the Ongoing phase. Choose Supervision or
Initial Intensive if that matches the mentee's phase.

132
00:17:30,560 --> 00:17:33,000
This tool includes advanced competencies.

133
00:17:33,560 --> 00:17:38,940
These are not required for a mentee
to be considered a competent provider.

134
00:17:40,980 --> 00:17:48,100
You can choose whether to assess them.

135
00:17:48,220 --> 00:17:57,980
They don't affect whether the
mentee is classified as competent.

136
00:18:02,320 --> 00:18:07,620
Advanced competencies are shaded grey,

137
00:18:08,920 --> 00:18:13,120
just as in the paper tool.

138
00:18:15,500 --> 00:18:20,700
Let's choose a couple of items,

139
00:18:22,560 --> 00:18:28,740
and this one, and skip the rest.

140
00:18:30,480 --> 00:18:33,140
With three items chosen,
we tap Confirm plan.

141
00:18:35,920 --> 00:18:39,760
We've already covered these steps.

142
00:18:43,540 --> 00:18:53,500
This mentee has been assessed before,
so each item shows its previous score.

143
00:18:53,840 --> 00:18:58,700
Last time, this item scored 1:
competency not demonstrated.

144
00:18:59,300 --> 00:19:04,220
Say they've improved this time, to a 4.

145
00:19:05,600 --> 00:19:09,680
The app flags that they've improved,

146
00:19:10,720 --> 00:19:15,180
compared with their score on 16 October.

147
00:19:16,800 --> 00:19:20,840
E3 scored 4 last time.

148
00:19:21,200 --> 00:19:23,200
Say it's now a 2.

149
00:19:23,740 --> 00:19:27,880
The app flags that they've
regressed, with a down arrow.

150
00:19:30,140 --> 00:19:32,400
This is the advanced item.

151
00:19:32,500 --> 00:19:37,120
Say it scored 2 last
time, and still scores 2.

152
00:19:38,360 --> 00:19:41,080
The app shows there's no change.

153
00:19:43,480 --> 00:19:50,160
I chose Echocardiogram because it has
this extra section, in the blue card.

154
00:19:51,600 --> 00:20:00,300
It's part of the paper tool,

155
00:20:00,480 --> 00:20:05,000
so the app includes it too, to match
the document as closely as possible.

156
00:20:05,940 --> 00:20:16,140
The first count is the number of
echocardiograms performed under supervision.

157
00:20:18,740 --> 00:20:21,840
Tap the plus button to add.

158
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:24,160
Let's say they performed two.

159
00:20:26,580 --> 00:20:29,400
Of those two, how many were correct?

160
00:20:30,840 --> 00:20:33,920
That is, how many reached
the correct final diagnosis?

161
00:20:34,620 --> 00:20:35,680
Let's say one.

162
00:20:37,800 --> 00:20:45,220
Use minus to decrease a count,
and plus to increase it.

163
00:20:49,380 --> 00:20:51,300
Session notes are optional.

164
00:20:52,320 --> 00:20:55,060
That's how the counts are recorded.

165
00:20:58,240 --> 00:21:01,020
Then tap Review session, below.

166
00:21:01,400 --> 00:21:08,880
The review lists the items that
haven't reached competency yet,

167
00:21:08,880 --> 00:21:12,980
including items from earlier plans that
weren't scored today, marked "Not scored".

168
00:21:17,180 --> 00:21:22,160
Below that are some basic statistics.

169
00:21:26,120 --> 00:21:28,700
Everything looks right,
so we tap Save Session.

170
00:21:34,420 --> 00:21:42,400
The mentee now has three sessions:
the two from before, plus this one.

171
00:21:43,260 --> 00:21:47,480
That's how monitoring works in the app.

172
00:21:50,760 --> 00:21:53,800
Let's go back.

173
00:21:54,760 --> 00:21:59,660
Next, I'd like to show syncing.

174
00:22:00,740 --> 00:22:09,980
We'll often be working in areas
with poor internet, or none at all.

175
00:22:13,320 --> 00:22:23,140
Once you're connected, the app syncs
automatically, or you can sync yourself.

176
00:22:25,020 --> 00:22:35,060
It does sync automatically, but it's good
practice to also sync manually, just to be sure.

177
00:22:35,400 --> 00:22:41,320
Tap the arrows in the header
to open the sync page.

178
00:22:43,560 --> 00:22:51,700
To sync only users, for example after
adding new mentees, tap Sync Users.

179
00:22:51,700 --> 00:22:58,100
After a session or evaluation,
sync sessions here.

180
00:22:58,100 --> 00:23:01,360
After adding a district,
tap Sync Districts.

181
00:23:01,940 --> 00:23:04,460
We'll tap Sync All.

182
00:23:07,300 --> 00:23:19,700
It shows "Synced successfully" once the data is
on the server, where administrators can see it.

183
00:23:21,520 --> 00:23:34,880
From then on, even if you lose your phone,
tablet or laptop, the data is safe on the server.

184
00:23:36,840 --> 00:23:49,400
Over time, you may record hundreds of
evaluations, and the device may slow down.

185
00:23:49,620 --> 00:23:52,020
If so, you can run Storage Cleanup here.

186
00:23:53,060 --> 00:24:00,620
It frees space on the device by removing old
sessions that are already safely on the server.

187
00:24:03,320 --> 00:24:17,160
It only clears completed journeys, and keeps
each journey's latest session on the device.

188
00:24:24,600 --> 00:24:34,620
Thank you for watching. If you have
any questions, please get in touch.
